  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 151 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nPrecipitation was slowly ending over the area this afternoon as the \nupper low makes northeast progress out of the state. Plenty of cloud \nand northwest winds behind it and this should be the rule through at \nleast the evening with some falling temps likely this afternoon on \nreasonable cold-air advection. A modest blocking regime aloft pushes \nthe low on north tonight into Wednesday with northwest winds \ncontinuing for a cooler day. Weakening upper energy from the west \nsplits under a modest high to its north and moves east into the \nsouthern and central Plains Wednesday night into Thursday. This \nbrings modest precipitation chances to the local area with an 80-90 \npercent chance of dry conditions remaining. The split upper flow \npattern continues into early next week with rather benign conditions \nand near normal temperatures.",
